      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "In order to study the role of nitric oxide (NO) during the airway inflammation of asthmatic rat, we investigated expression of inducible nitric oxide synthase (iNOS) in the lung tissue of asthmatic rats."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Animal model of asthmatic Wistar rats was developed by being sensitized and challenged with ovalbumin. Activities of iNOS were measured by using SP immunohistochemical method."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "In asthmatic rat group (n = 10), lung tissue showed stronger immunostaining (90%) for iNOS than control group (20%) (P < 0.001). Immunostaining was mainly present in the bronchial epithelium, alveolar epithelium, bronchial smooth muscle, vascular endothelial and smooth muscle cells and inflammatory cells such as macrophages and neutrophils. In glucocorticoid treated group (n = 10), there was down regulation of iNOS immunoreactivity (30% positive) compared with control asthmatic rat group (20%)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "The increased expression of iNOS in asthmatic rat lung tissue showed NO playing a critical role in asthmatic inflammation, otherwise expression of iNOS was inhibited by glucocorticoid."
        }
      ]},
